A||N||2||zoie||Turn signal lever 1988 2m4||||9||
Z||000000||zoie||09-10-2000||06:33 PM||||Are the 1984-88 2m4 turn signal levers without cruise interchangeable with singal levers that have cruise control?  I don't use the cruise control but need to replace the broken lever at a reasonable cost. How difficult is the change out?  <P>------------------<BR>||||reg||9
Z||000001||mrfiero||09-10-2000||07:26 PM||||Yes, although you will obviously lose your cruise control.  Grab the stalk and pull it straight out.  It should just pop out, but I've had a few that were stubborn.  You'll have to unplug the wiring under the dash to and feed it through the column, but it's not that difficult.  <P>I have a good used stalk with the cruise switch if you decide to go that route, but a regular stalk will at least be functional for the turn signals and wipers.  ||||reg||10
Z||000002||Monkeyman||09-10-2000||08:39 PM||||<B>WAIT!!!!</B>  <P>If you decide to replace your CC stalk with another CC stalk, may I suggest that you clip the wires at the stalk 1st?  I pulled my broken CC stalk out and replaced it with a non-CC stalk (too stupid to think about gluing it <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">) and now that I have a working CC stalk, I've found that I'll have to do tons of work to get the wiring threaded back through the steering column.  If you leave the wiring, you might be able to tape the plug on the new one to what's left of the old one and pull it through that way.<P>Sorry for the bandwidth, but I'd hate to see someone else go through this.||||reg||1
